title: Make public or unlisted room-history readability a persisted room setting
---
B111 established that public and unlisted room history is currently anonymously readable solely from room visibility. Make history readability a separate, persisted per-room policy.

Required policy:
- public and unlisted rooms may set history_public true or false; anonymous room-history reads are permitted only when true.
- gated and private rooms must always have history_public=false and remain member-only.
- changing a room to gated/private atomically clears history_public (or rejects the change until false; prefer atomic clear).
- existing/new public and unlisted rooms should default true for compatible rollout; gated/private default false.

Acceptance criteria:
- Persist the setting across restart in both InMemoryRelay and SQLite paths, including a safe migration.
- Add a member-authorized, signed mutation whose boolean is included in canonical signed bytes.
- Anonymous /room_history passes/fails correctly for public/unlisted based on setting; a valid member can still read a history-closed listed room.
- Setting history_public=true for gated/private fails.
- Update relay landing/help copy and add InMemory, SQLite, signed-op, and HTTP matrix coverage.

Source seams: relay_backend_contract, relay.ml room persistence/handle_room_history, relay_signed_ops, relay_sqlite_support. Evidence: B111 audit.